Sval: one data directory, with no profile database or profile manager

Sval keeps its data in one directory, `Data` in the application's data
directory (toolkit/profile/SvalDataDirectory.cpp). The profile service knows
it as its only profile and the default of every install, and never reads or
writes profiles.ini or installs.ini. That database gives each install
location a profile of its own, which would start Sval with none of its data
whenever it runs from another path, and holds the ShowSelector flag that
opens the profile group selector on every launch.

ShowProfileManager refuses to open, so `-P`, `-ProfileManager` and
`XRE_RESTART_TO_PROFILE_MANAGER` exit with a message. `--profile <path>`
still starts Sval on another directory.

A background task that keeps its own profile keeps it in the tasks'
directory under its install-and-task prefix, with no salt and no record in
the database.

Selecting the default profile creates its directory, which Firefox's
database otherwise guarantees exists.

